{"title":"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A large bag of coins contains pennies, dimes and quarters. There are twice as many dimes as pennies and three times as many quarters as dimes. An amount of money which could be in the bag is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d60cfdac53bffa56e45ddd82444f2b9a753b314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ } \\$306 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }  \\$333 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)\\ } \\$342 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\  }  \\$348 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\  }  \\$360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"478\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> pennies in the bag, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> dimes and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb9d29e70ac2c4f2c31e1a15a37f946bb6004213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(2x) = 6x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> quarters. Since pennies are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46b66729b2443c4ecd87e2267df87d38f4a8bc57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.01$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, dimes are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/9/df9ecc46380162cef40875158c3e20173a9355cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, and quarters are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbcfc22da43fe3886c3ff0069a4ade504c70d307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, the total amount of money in the bag is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/265fd948ce338422abfceaa1a1b75e28cf47bda6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\$ \\left(0.01x+(0.10)(2x)+(0.25)(6x)\\right) = \\$1.71x.\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"18\" /> Therefore, the possible amounts of money are precisely the integer multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/9/71964b7b07f90c0dc33389b8ddbe8e348243587a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.71$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>Since the answer choices are all integer numbers of dollars, we multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> to deduce that the answer must be an integer multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/584787f7c02825aef82978d8355fb37ddf14dc3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$171$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" />. The only such multiple among the answer choices is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/d/31db2513db1898a70ab8ed9e89a2a46fc497964a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$(2 \\cdot 171) = \\boxed{\\text{(C)} \\ \\$342}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"177\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME\" title=\"1985 AHSME\">1985 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1985 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 AHSME Proble